17393,80fc015bdfe1f5b870c1e1ee02d78e709523fee7,CVE-2009-3623,2009.0,CWE-287,Permission,"nfsd4: use common rpc_cred for all callbacks

Callbacks are always made using the machine's identity, so we can use a
single auth_generic credential shared among callbacks to all clients and
let the rpc code take care of the rest.

Signed-off-by: J. Bruce Fields <bfields@citi.umich.edu>","// File path: fs/nfsd/nfs4callback.c
nfsd4_cb_recall(struct nfs4_delegation *dp)
{
	struct nfs4_client *clp = dp->dl_client;
	struct rpc_clnt *clnt = clp->cl_cb_conn.cb_client;
	struct rpc_message msg = {
		.rpc_proc = &nfs4_cb_procedures[NFSPROC4_CLNT_CB_RECALL],
		.rpc_argp = dp,
		.rpc_cred = clp->cl_cb_conn.cb_cred
	};
	int status;

